When a portfolio item says "ACT NOW: Cache or materialize QUERY_FINGERPRINT abc123," clicking it should open the Entity 360 view for that fingerprint, showing all related context (cost history, execution patterns, related alerts).

*Reasoning:* The decision to act requires investigation. The investigation tool (Entity 360) exists on another page. A deep link completes the flow: prioritize → investigate → decide → act.

**30. SLO breaches should create ACTIONS automatically.**
When an SLO breaches, it should auto-create an ACTION_QUEUE item: "Investigate SLO breach: WAREHOUSE_P95_SEC > 5s on WH_ALFA_QUERY. Source: SLO objective #7." This connects the objective system to the action system.

*Reasoning:* SLOs that breach without creating work items are unaccountable. Auto-creating actions ensures every breach has an owner and a tracking artifact.

**31. The Scenarios section should pull VERIFIED savings from the Cost > Savings ledger and show ROI.**
The Scenarios section projects future savings. But it doesn't show: "To date, Decision Studio recommendations have been implemented and verified at $X/quarter." This is the tool's own ROI.

*Reasoning:* If you can't prove the tool's recommendations generated real value, the tool is just a planning toy. Verified savings from past recommendations ARE the proof.

**32. Cost Truth should have a "drill into the gap" action — jump to the specific unattributed service.**
When Cost Truth shows "$3,200 unattributed in serverless," there should be a link to: "See serverless detail on Cost & Contract > Spend & Attribution" — a one-click cross-page navigation to investigate.

*Reasoning:* Identifying a gap without a path to investigate it creates frustration. "Here's the gap; click here to understand it" completes the analytical flow.

